%description:

Tcp.windowScalingFactor:invalid -- a factor above 14 stops the run with an error.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "Valid values are 0..14, and -1 for automatic selection".

The classes: auto (-1, the default), explicit (0 to 14), invalid (below -1 or above 14),
too-small (a factor that cannot represent advertisedWindow). The code:
TcpConnection::configureStateVariables() checks the value, and the options of the SYN select
the factor.

Host under test: host1. Observation: the error, and the exit code of the run.

%# parameter: Tcp.windowScalingFactor
%# class: invalid
%# value: 15
%# key: *.host1.tcp.windowScalingFactor
%# expected-result: PASS

%activity:
EV << "TcpWindowScalingFactorInvalid compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.windowScalingFactor = 15    # the parameter under test
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%exitcode: 1

%contains-regex: stderr
Invalid parameter value windowScalingFactor=15
